From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:26:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: name the retained-gadget s2idle precheck refusal

Log why the retained-gadget precheck refused (not-s2idle or
gadget-not-peripheral, with op_state), only during a suspend attempt.
The decision is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
index fabee8363..0a2aa1058 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
@@ -689,8 +689,15 @@ static int dwc2_sleep_precheck(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action,
 	if (device_property_read_bool(dwc2->dev, "apple,retain-gadget-in-s2idle") &&
 	    (action != PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE ||
 	     (dwc2->op_state != OTG_STATE_B_PERIPHERAL &&
-	      dwc2->op_state != OTG_STATE_B_IDLE)))
+	      dwc2->op_state != OTG_STATE_B_IDLE))) {
+		/* Only for an attempt: the readiness query polls this. */
+		if (data == PM_SUSPEND_PRECHECK_ATTEMPT)
+			dev_info(dwc2->dev, "system sleep refused: %s op_state=%d\n",
+				 action != PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE ? "not-s2idle" :
+								"gadget-not-peripheral",
+				 dwc2->op_state);
 		return notifier_from_errno(-EBUSY);
+	}
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
 
